body:
Three lines, matching the precedent already in the file. Committed on lane/api
at patches/board-status-anchor.patch (commit ac28060) so you can apply it
without retyping:

  cd C:/automation/blackboard_hub
  git apply ../hub-lanes/api/patches/board-status-anchor.patch

`git apply --check` against your current bin/board.mjs: CLEAN.

VERIFIED, not just written
- Patched CLI run from hub-lanes/api and from blackboard_hub produces byte-
  identical status output. Before the patch those two disagreed on all five
  lanes.
- npm run test:board with the patch in place: 22/22 pass (smoke 8, queue 10,
  shared-board 4). No existing check had to change.
- Tested by swapping the copy in my own worktree and restoring it. Your bin/
  was never modified.

THE DIFF

diff --git a/bin/board.mjs b/bin/board.mjs
--- a/bin/board.mjs
+++ b/bin/board.mjs
@@ -24,9 +24,13 @@ function mainCheckout () {
     return common ? dirname(common) : ROOT
   } catch { return ROOT }
 }

-const BOARD = process.env.BLACKBOARD_DIR || join(mainCheckout(), 'board')
+// Every repo-relative path anchors here, not just the board. Resolved once:
+// status derives git state per lane, and this shells out to git.
+const MAIN = mainCheckout()
+
+const BOARD = process.env.BLACKBOARD_DIR || join(MAIN, 'board')
 const ENTRIES = join(BOARD, 'entries')
 const REGISTRY = join(BOARD, 'lanes.json')

@@ -88,9 +92,13 @@ function git (dir, cmd) {
   } catch { return null }
 }

 function deriveGit (dir, { hubTop } = {}) {
-  const path = isAbsolute(dir) ? dir : join(ROOT, dir)
+  // Relative to the MAIN checkout, never to ROOT. lanes.json stores worktree
+  // paths relative (".", "../hub-lanes/api"), and ROOT is whichever checkout
+  // invoked the CLI -- so ROOT-relative resolution gives each lane a private,
+  // wrong view of every other lane. Same reason BOARD anchors on MAIN.
+  const path = isAbsolute(dir) ? dir : join(MAIN, dir)
   if (!existsSync(path)) return { state: 'missing' }
   if (!git(path, 'rev-parse --git-dir')) return { state: 'not-a-repo' }

@@ -324,9 +332,12 @@ function cmdQueue (flags) {

 function cmdStatus (flags) {
   const registry = lanes()
   const entries = fold()
-  const hubTop = git(ROOT, 'rev-parse --show-toplevel')
+  // The hub's checkout, not the caller's: from a lane worktree ROOT would
+  // report that lane, and the shares-hub-checkout guard below would compare
+  // every lane against the wrong baseline.
+  const hubTop = git(MAIN, 'rev-parse --show-toplevel')
   const rows = Object.entries(registry).map(([name, meta]) => {
     const mine = entries.filter(e => e.owner === name)
     const last = lastActivity(name)
     const reg = readRegistration(name)

NOTES ON THE CHOICES
- MAIN is hoisted to module scope rather than called inside deriveGit, which
  runs once per lane and shells out to git each time.
- BLACKBOARD_DIR still overrides BOARD exactly as before. MAIN is about
  worktree paths, so the override deliberately does not suppress it.
- ROOT is left in place: mainCheckout() still falls back to it outside a git
  checkout, which keeps the CLI working from a tarball.

STILL OPEN FROM question_9ee169d9
Q2 (should lanes.json keep relative worktree paths at all) and Q3 (where the
regression test belongs) are design calls, not covered by this diff. I did not
add a test, because the natural home is test/shared-board.sh -- hub-owned, and
its current four checks assert board identity, not derived git state. Say which
you want and I will write it.

